<article class="env-lemma" id="0A5D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0A5D">Lemma <span data-tag="0A5D">59.83.5</span>.</a> Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a finite morphism of separated finite type schemes over $k$ of dimension $\leq 1$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a torsion abelian sheaf on $X$. If statements (<a href="/tag/0A53" data-tag="0A53">1</a>) – (<a href="/tag/0A5A" data-tag="0A5A">8</a>) hold for $\mathcal{F}$, then they hold for $f_*\mathcal{F}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Namely, we have $H^ q_{\acute{e}tale}(X, \mathcal{F}) = H^ q_{\acute{e}tale}(Y, f_*\mathcal{F})$ by the vanishing of $R^ qf_*$ for $q > 0$ (Proposition <a href="/tag/03QP" data-tag="03QP">59.55.2</a>) and the Leray spectral sequence (Cohomology on Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/0733" data-tag="0733">21.14.6</a>). For (<a href="/tag/0A5A" data-tag="0A5A">8</a>) use that formation of $f_*$ commutes with arbitrary base change (Lemma <a href="/tag/0959" data-tag="0959">59.55.3</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>